From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: krane <chris@krane.dev>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 17:13:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(system-info): prefer the discrete GPU in the lspci
 fallback

Backport of pctrade/end4-pC ebeef46
https://github.com/pctrade/end4-pC/commit/ebeef46
Problem: the lspci fallback took the first display controller, usually the iGPU, and the space left before "(rev xx)" stopped the bracket extraction from matching.
Port: clean (offset)
Drop when: the pinned getGpu picks a non-Intel controller first and strips the space before "(rev xx)".
---
 dots/.config/quickshell/ii/services/SystemInfo.qml | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/services/SystemInfo.qml b/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/services/SystemInfo.qml
index 5c0a30ba..ff25e57f 100644
--- a/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/services/SystemInfo.qml
+++ b/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/services/SystemInfo.qml
@@ -145,9 +145,13 @@ Singleton {
         command: ["bash", "-c", `
             gpu=$(glxinfo 2>/dev/null | grep 'renderer string' | grep -o 'Intel(R) HD Graphics [0-9]\\{4\\}' | sed 's/Intel(R)/Intel®/')
             if [ -z "$gpu" ]; then
-                gpu=$(lspci | grep -iE 'vga|3d|display' | head -1 | sed -E '
+                # Prefer a discrete card: the iGPU usually sits first on the bus
+                gpus=$(lspci | grep -iE 'vga|3d|display')
+                line=$(echo "$gpus" | grep -vi 'Intel Corporation' | head -1)
+                [ -z "$line" ] && line=$(echo "$gpus" | head -1)
+                gpu=$(echo "$line" | sed -E '
                     s/.*: //;
-                    s/\\(rev [0-9a-f]+\\)//;
+                    s/ *\\(rev [0-9a-f]+\\)//;
                     s/Advanced Micro Devices, Inc\\. \\[AMD\\/ATI\\]//;
                     s/NVIDIA Corporation//;
                     s/Intel Corporation//;
